def max_sum_pair_diff_lessthan_K(arr, K, k):
    arr.sort()  # Sort the array to make it easier to find pairs
    sum_val = 0  # Variable to store the sum of the pairs
    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1  # Two pointers to start and end of the array

    while left < right:
        # Check if the sum of the current pair is equal to or less than K and also check if the sum of the pair is greater than k divisible by k
        if arr[left] + arr[right] <= K and (arr[left] + arr[right]) % k != 0:
            sum_val += (arr[left] + arr[right])  # Add the sum of the pair to the total sum
            left += 1  # Move the left pointer to the right
            right -= 1  # Move the right pointer to the left
        else:
            if arr[left] + arr[right] > K:
                right -= 1  # Move the right pointer to the left
            else:
                left += 1  # Move the left pointer to the right

    return sum_val  # Return the total sum of the pairs
```
This function first sorts the array to make it easier to find pairs. It then uses two pointers, one starting at the beginning of the array and the other at the end, moving towards the center. If the sum of the current pair is equal to or less than K and also greater than k divisible by k, it adds the sum to the total sum. If the sum of the current pair is greater than K, the right pointer is moved to the left, otherwise, the left pointer is moved to the right. This process continues until the pointers meet in the middle.

