import heapq

def maximum_product(arr):
    # Use a heap to keep track of the top three largest numbers
    largest = [-float('inf')] * 3
    for num in arr:
        heapq.heappush(largest, num)
        if len(largest) > 3:
            heapq.heappop(largest)

    # The maximum product will be the product of the three largest numbers
    return heapq.heappop(largest) * heapq.heappop(largest) * heapq.heappop(largest)
```

In this solution, we use a max-heap to efficiently keep track of the three largest numbers in the array. The `heapq` module provides an implementation of the heap queue algorithm, which is particularly useful for this problem. The `-float('inf')` values in the heap represent negative infinity, so that any number pushed into the heap will automatically become the new maximum. After finding the three largest numbers, we multiply them together to get the maximum product.

